# Keep the vendored coastline byte-identical on every platform.
#
# It is hashed, and its digest is recorded in each gridded database's manifest
# so a map cannot be drawn against a shoreline the data was not built against.
# Left to git's text handling, core.autocrlf gives a Windows checkout CRLF and
# a Linux one LF, the file hashes two ways, and the check fires on a
# difference that is not a difference. frer.landmask normalises newlines
# before hashing too; this keeps the working copies themselves in agreement.
*.geojson text eol=lf

# The committed design-value database and its manifest, for the same reason:
# they are compared byte-for-byte against rebuilds.
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.gz binary
